 "findings": {
  "numbering_tab_separated": "bullets, decimal, alpha and roman levels separated by a tab render with every metric identical to the typed form; printed numbers equal the source's across an interrupted list",
  "numbering_run_in": "w:suff space/nothing is not honoured: Docs draws a tab where the space was, setting the text about 0.5in past the label's indent (c1: indent 69.9pt, text 106.0pt), so run-in '1. text' items land right of the source (probe_nested justified items 97.7 -> 106.9pt; c1_whitepaper recommendations 79.6 -> 106.0pt). Those lists stay typed under gdocs (structures.numbering_plan tab_only)",
  "footnotes": "withheld: real notes sit at the foot of the text area (probe_footnotes dy_p90 3.33 -> 73.87pt) and custom marks are renumbered (a '*' mark and a restart at 1 print as continuing automatic numbers)"
 },
